  "details": "There are four world favourite tabs each holding 32 favourited worlds.  For a total of 128 worlds.\nPeople use there favourite worlds tab for different reasons some use it for cool worlds they find, others use it for events.\nEventually they fill up,  now if you want to keep reference to the favourited worlds after you remove them from your tabs your only option is to either write them down on paper or alt tab to notepad and try and store them there.\nThis is also what you need to do if you want to share a list of worlds you favourited in one go.\nSo here is my suggestion.  Add the ability in the settings menu where you can clear your cashe to export your favourite worlds tabs.\nThis will create a text file in a vrchat folder in your documents folder that contains the details of all your favourited worlds at the time you exported them.\nThis text file contains the details of each world its title,  world author and world ID in a handy numbered list.\nYou can then remove your favourited worlds from your tabs knowing there saved in that text file.\nEach time you export it creates a new text file with the date and time in the title so you know when they where made.\nThis is list is not only handy for storing old favourited worlds but also for sharing a list of worlds you find between people.\nI think this would be a handy feature.",
